DESCRIPTION:<p><strong>Wake Audubon Monthly Meeting:</strong> </p><p><b><
 i>(Meeting is usually In Person and Zoom\, but check back for updates!)</i
 ></b></p><p>Time: <strong>Second Tuesday of the month</strong>\, 7:30 - 9:
 00 pm<br>Nature Research Center\, 121 W. Jones St\, Raleigh\, NC 27601</p>
 <p><br>Place: In-person + Virtual via Zoom <br>Location: NC Museum of Nat
 ural Sciences: Nature Research Center\, 121 W Jones St\, Raleigh\, NC - 4t
 h floor meeting room</p><p>Location: In-person + Zoom (Note:<i> The two s
 peakers will be on Zoom</i> )<br>Place: In-person + Virtual - use <a hre
 f="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.zoom.us/join&amp\;sa=D&amp\;so
 urce=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw2pLih8fe1aJ9TBTDzjAZYv" target="_b
 lank"><u>https://www.zoom.us/join</u></a>  \, choose &quot\;Join meeting&
 quot\; (no login needed)</p><ul><li>Meeting code: <strong>831 3786 5298</
 strong></li><li>Password: <strong>4Birds</strong></li></ul><p>Park (for f
 ree after 6:30 pm) and walk to the main museum entrance on Jones Street\,
  <strong>just to the right of the giant globe.</strong> <b><i>Since the 
 NC Museum of Natural Sciences is usually closed at night\, someone will be
  at the door ONLY from 7 to 7:45 to let you in\, so please be on time.</i>
 </b> Take the elevator to the fourth floor meeting room. The east-facing e
 ntrance of the &quot\;old wing&quot\; of the museum will not be used. If y
 ou feel unwell\, please stay home and enjoy our presentation over Zoom</p>
 <p>We hope you will help us by joining Wake Audubon and National Audubon!<
 br>visit <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=http://wakeaudubon.org&amp\
 ;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw33Yly6IqDRSWuLSs7lVQb
 P" target="_blank">wakeaudubon.org</a></p><p>*Last updated 2025-07-17 by B
 eegle<br>WATCH for updates. Location and date sometime change!</p>
