BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_newhopeaudubon
SUMMARY:NHBA Bird Outing
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260715T070000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260715T100000
DTSTAMP:20260712T033936Z
UID:6p2l90lserltmfcnpv7bqbj2bf@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260715T070000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260626T154155Z
DESCRIPTION:For questions\, contact Ross McKinney at <a href="mailto:ros
 smck@mindspring.com" target="_blank"><u>rossmck@mindspring.com</u></a>. Th
 e location will be Sandy Creek Park\, 3510 Sandy Creek Dr\, Durham\, NC 27
 707. This is an accessible site with paved trails. <a href="https://audubo
 n.maps.arcgis.com/apps/webappviewer/index.html?id=b9d1bd41b4f1429f867f3308
 85e2250e&amp\;query=Birdability_ReCreation_Public_View_9655\,what_is_the_n
 ame_of_the_area_tr\,Sandy%20Creek%20Park">See more information here on acc
 essibility.</a> <br><br>This outing is sponsored by the New Hope Bird All
 iance (formerly New Hope Audubon).<br><br>Outings usually last 2-3 hours. 
 No reservations or sign-up needed. If there is a large turnout for any par
 ticular outing\, we may split into two groups. We do recommend carpooling 
 for families or friend pods\; while we love pets\, there is a ‘no-pet’
  policy for bird outings. New birders and birders of all skill levels are 
 welcome. <br><br>Please wear long pants\, socks\, and sturdy shoes (ticks 
 and chiggers may be present). Sun and bug protection are also recommended.
  Bring snacks and water if you like. Heavy rain will result in cancellatio
 n.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260626T154155Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:New Hope Bird Alliance
END:VEVENT
