UID:122667-1784122200-1784125800@www.naturalsciences.org
SUMMARY:Purple Martin Week: The Swallows - Avian Aeronautical Marvels
DESCRIPTION:Photo by John Gerwin \nSwallows refer to a group of insectivorous birds with some phenomenal flight abilities. Various species have been prominent in the stories of ancient cultures\, and continue to fascinate us today. \nSwallows are songbirds that occur worldwide. There are ~90 species described\, and as a group\, swallows can be found almost anywhere on the planet\, including over Antarctica once in a while. Many species are migratory and this is the case for those found in the U.S. 6 species breed in North Carolina – one of these only in a few NC locations. \nFor this talk\, John will discuss and show pictures of these 8 species\, focusing on those 6 that breed in NC; how one might go about seeing them; how to attract some; and\, to give equal time\, how to dissuade them (a pair nesting on your porch can be messy). He has even promised\, or threatened as it were\, to consider this existential question: “What is the airspeed velocity of an unladen swallow?” \nPlease join us to learn more about airspeed velocity and other curious features about the lives of North Carolina’s swallows. \nOur Expert \nJohn Gerwin\, Research Curator of Ornithology at NCMNS
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/purple-martin-week-the-swallows-avian-aeronautical-marvels/
LOCATION:Nature Research Center\, 121 West Jones Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adults,General Events,K-12 Students,Lectures,Meet the Scientist,SECU Daily Planet Theater,Walk-up Programs
ORGANIZER;CN="Chris%20Smith":MAILTO:christopher.smith@naturalsciences.org
GEO:35.7822405;-78.6409677
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Nature Research Center 121 West Jones Street Raleigh NC 27601 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=121 West Jones Street:geo:-78.6409677,35.7822405
END:VEVENT
