CREATED:20260624T235601Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>This event to hosted by Sapphic Social! Reach out to allis
 on@sapphic.social  with any questions.</b><br><br>Looking to learn how to
  do your femme’s makeup? Or maybe learn a new style? Or even maybe you
 ’re entirely new to makeup and don’t know where to start? <br><br>Com
 e join us as we cover:<br>- Starting base for foundation application<br>-
  Concealer\, contour\, blush and highlighting application<br>- Eyeshadow
 /optional cut crease tutorial<br>- Winged eyeliner technique<br>- False 
 lash application<br>- Makeup removal (optional)<br><br><u>This event is e
 ntirely free to attend\, all we ask is that you bring your own materials. 
 For this class\, you will need to bring the following:</u><br>- Full brush
  set\, for an example of what this includes\, check out this link: <a hre
 f="https://sy-beauty.com/makeup-brushes-names-and-their-uses/" target="_bl
 ank"><u>https://sy-beauty.com/makeup-brushes-names-and-their-uses/</u></a>
 <br>- Foundation and concealer in your shade<br>- Blush<br>- Bronzer<br
 >- Highlight<br>- Eyeliner<br>- Eyeshadow palette of your choice (must 
 have white or nude included for cut crease tutorial)<br>- False lashes of
  your choice and eyelash glue<br><br><br><b>Please wash your face and mois
 turize before arrival for best results! </b>You will be provided your own
  angled brush(es)\, primer (E.L.F grip)\, makeup remover and cotton pads.<
 br><br><br><b>We will also be collecting donations for the LGBT Center Of 
 Durham during the event! If you’d like to donate\, go for it! Anything i
 s appreciated :)</b>
