UID:event_315537455@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260712T033917Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260723T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260723T233000
SUMMARY:Thursday Community Board Game night at Moondog Meadery
DESCRIPTION:Durham Geeks\nIn conjunction with Moon Dog Meadery\, we contin
 ue to have our Thursday Night Gaming Night from 7 until they kick us out. 
 It's a bit smaller group than the large Monday night extravaganza\, and th
 ere are a lot of drop in and independent groups here as well. Restaurants 
 are open on Thursdays\, so you can Dash you food right inside\, or bring i
 t with you!\n\nMoondog has an extensive and ever-changing collection of ga
 mes that are usually loaned out for a fee\, but on Thursdays (just like on
  Mondays)\, they are all free to play. Usually we can find folks to fill i
 n your table or teach you the basics of the games. I've been hosting it fo
 r a few months now\, and we have had a great time with students returning 
 and bringing in new colleagues\, as well as the faithful ones who attended
  over the summer.\n\nDogs and outside food both allowed and encouraged. Al
 ways free! There is award-winning mead on tap and bottled\, as well as an 
 ever-changing collection of beer\, cider\, THC-infused water\, colas and\,
  yes\, just plain old water to keep you hydrated on your adventure.\n\nAny
  questions? Contact us here at Durham Geeks!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/durham-geeks/events/315537455/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260703T232257Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260703T232257Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncwf": "https://ncwf.org/event/bat-discovery-program-swannanoa/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncwf
X-SOURCE:NC Wildlife Federation
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260723T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260723T223000
DTSTAMP:20260711T233935
CREATED:20260512T160825Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260512T160826Z
UID:10001618-1784833200-1784845800@ncwf.org
SUMMARY:Bat Discovery Program (Swannanoa)
DESCRIPTION:Please join Swannanoa Valley WILD! for a special Bat Discovery Program at Warren Wilson College with Wildlife Biologist Scott Fletcher. Did you know North Carolina is home to at least 17 different species of bats? Often overlooked due to their nocturnal nature\, these amazing ecosystem warriors will be out and about during the waxing moon. Come take advantage of this opportunity to learn more about your tiny neighbors\, the only flying mammals on the planet! \nPlease feel free to bring folding chairs or a blanket to sit on\, a head lamp or flashlight\, bug spray\, water and snacks. And as always\, bring your curiosity! Scott will bring the latest in bat identification technology such as thermal cameras and bat acoustic monitors. The event is free and open to all\, but registration is required. \nScott holds a Bachelor of Science in wildlife biology from the University of Maine and a Master’s degree in environmental management from Duke University. He is a Certified Wildlife Biologist and was a Professional Wetland Scientist. Scott has 41 years of experience in wildlife\, endangered species\, wetlands\, habitat restoration\, general environmental impact analyses and assessments\, and federal\, state\, and local natural resource policy and permitting activities.  \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/bat-discovery-program-swannanoa/
CATEGORIES:Featured
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncwf.org/wp-content/uploads/batty.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
