BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncwf": "https://ncwf.org/event/moth-night-durham/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncwf
X-SOURCE:NC Wildlife Federation
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260724T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260724T230000
DTSTAMP:20260711T233935
CREATED:20260626T180239Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260626T180239Z
UID:10001654-1784923200-1784934000@ncwf.org
SUMMARY:Moth Night (Durham)
DESCRIPTION:NCWF Durham Wildlife Stewards Chapter is thrilled to present its first-ever Moth Night\, in conjunction with Backyard Butterflies of Hillsborough. We will learn how to photograph moths and upload the photos to iNaturalist. The photos will eventually become research-grade data for scientists to use. We will circulate around three to four moth light trapping stations that are set up along the trails and lit to attract moths. Moths will be continually flying onto the sheets and back off again\, so you’ll see something different every time. The focus is not on identifying each moth by its scientific name\, but instead on documenting through photography all the moths and insects that land on the sheet. Since you’ll see the moths change position\, disappear\, and reappear every second\, what better way to live in the moment? \nCome moth with us! Discover the mysterious nighttime world of moths\, and be a citizen scientist who uploads their observations to iNaturalist. Your observations will become part of the first-ever moth survey at Sandy Creek Park! \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/moth-night-durham/
CATEGORIES:Featured
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncwf.org/wp-content/uploads/DWSmoths.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncwf": "https://ncwf.org/event/moth-night-carolina-beach/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncwf
X-SOURCE:NC Wildlife Federation
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260724T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260724T220000
DTSTAMP:20260711T233935
CREATED:20260317T175400Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260317T175401Z
UID:10001531-1784925000-1784930400@ncwf.org
SUMMARY:Moth Night (Carolina Beach)
DESCRIPTION:Join NCWF at Carolina Beach State Park for National Moth Week! Meet some moths you may have never seen before and listen for nocturnal birds in the coastal fringe forest of southeastern NC. Learn to use Seek and iNaturalist to identify and record species sightings. Upload 10 species observations to get your NC Moth Week badge! \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/moth-night-carolina-beach/
CATEGORIES:Featured
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncwf.org/wp-content/uploads/mothnightCBSP-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
