BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_newhopeaudubon
SUMMARY:NHBA Bird Outing
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260726T070000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260726T100000
DTSTAMP:20260712T033936Z
UID:2tfp6dbs4984hvtvhpas3qe4c3@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260726T070000
SEQUENCE:1
CREATED:20260626T155300Z
DESCRIPTION:For questions\, contact Joe Donahue at joe_donahue@bellsouth.
 net. The location will be Eno River State Park – Few’s Ford Access. 61
 01 Cole Mill Road\, Durham. Drive straight into the park and go to the par
 king loop/area at the end of the entry road. \n\nThis outing is sponsored
  by the New Hope Bird Alliance (formerly New Hope Audubon).\n\nOutings usu
 ally last 2-3 hours. No reservations or sign-up needed. If there is a larg
 e turnout for any particular outing\, we may split into two groups. We do 
 recommend carpooling for families or friend pods\; while we love pets\, th
 ere is a ‘no-pet’ policy for bird outings. New birders and birders of 
 all skill levels are welcome. \n\nPlease wear long pants\, socks\, and stu
 rdy shoes (ticks and chiggers may be present). Sun and bug protection are 
 also recommended. Bring snacks and water if you like. Heavy rain will resu
 lt in cancellation.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260703T195158Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:New Hope Bird Alliance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_wakeaudubon
SUMMARY:Bass Lake Park Birding
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260726T081500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260726T103000
DTSTAMP:20260712T033945Z
UID:4csdotgabcd1f200fcko342v9v@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260726T081500
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260609T154314Z
DESCRIPTION:Join Jessica W and  Wake Audubon for a Bird Outing at Bass La
 ke on <b>Sunday\, APRIL 26\, 2026\,  8:15 </b><br>The park opens at 8 am
 . The address is <b>900 Bass Lake Road\, Holly Springs\, NC</b> (note that
  this is the main parking lot\, not the smaller lot on another road). Meet
  at the end of the parking lot near the building. This  2+ mile walk on u
 npaved trails begins at 8:15 and ends shortly after 10:30. <br>**This out
 ing is on soft trails. We might cover the east side of the lake and then w
 alk to the adjacent Sugg Farm\, which is also part of Bass Lake Park. Wear
  shoes that can take a bit of mud as the trail if it has rained recently.<
 br>Leader is Jessica Williams (<a href="mailto:jesswilliams888@gmail.com" 
 target="_blank">jesswilliams888@gmail.com</a>\, 913-424-5062).
LAST-MODIFIED:20260609T154315Z
LOCATION:900 Bass Lake Rd\, Holly Springs\, NC 27540\, USA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-SOURCE:Wake Audubon
END:VEVENT
