DESCRIPTION:Engaged Defenders for Democracy<br> <br>Come join us every Th
 ursday from 7:30-9 am at American Tobacco Trail Bridge over I-40. Location
 : AMC Streets of Southpoint 8030 Renaissance Pkwy Durham\, NC 27713. . Par
 king lots are behind Southpoint Mall near the AMC theater or in the parkin
 g lot of Roses lot on Hwy 54. Go behind Southpoint Mall to the AMC theater
  parking lot. Walk towards Hwy 40 and look for entrance to the trail. It i
 s a 4-minute walk. You also can park at Rose's\, 105 W NC. Hwy 54 27713. T
 he walk to the bridge from Roses is a 4-minute walk.<br><br>We will have a
  big sign. If you bring signs\, please make sure they are positive and sho
 w what we are fighting for: "Freedom 4 All" "Protect Free Speech." Please 
 bring American flags to wave as well.<br><br>See you every Thursday mornin
 g engaging drivers &amp\; pedestrians  in Durham! <br><br>Please join our 
 Substack: <a href="https://substack.com/@engageddefendersfordemocracy?utm
 _source=global-search">https://substack.com/@engageddefendersfordemocracy?
 utm_source=global-search</a><br><br>For more ED4D Mobilize Events: <a hre
 f="https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfordemocracy/?show_all_events=tr
 ue">https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfordemocracy/</a><br><br><a hre
 f="https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfordemocracy/event/842835/" targ
 et="_blank">https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfordemocracy/event/8428
 35/</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260306T223224Z
LOCATION:8030 Renaissance Pkwy\, Durham\, NC\, 27713
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Durham Resistance (In Person)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncwf": "https://ncwf.org/event/cerulean-warbler-avian-diversity-study-9/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncwf
X-SOURCE:NC Wildlife Federation
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260730T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260730T160000
DTSTAMP:20260711T233935
CREATED:20260317T181650Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260317T181650Z
UID:10001545-1785398400-1785427200@ncwf.org
SUMMARY:Cerulean Warbler & Avian Diversity Study
DESCRIPTION:Join North Carolina Wildlife Federation\, National Parks Conservation Association\, the Center for Biological Diversity\, Defenders of Wildlife\, MountainTrue\, and the N.C. Wildlife Resources Commission with support from the U.S. Forest Service to help with a cerulean warbler and avian diversity survey project focused on the last remaining patches of old-growth forests and maturing second-growth forests within the Craggie Mountains – Pisgah National Forest where presence of ceruleans and many other avian species is largely unknown. \nOur goal is to fill area-specific knowledge gaps to provide best available information for future decision making in forest management and conservation efforts. To achieve this goal\, we are using acoustic recording units (ARUs). The units are mounted to trees within suitable habitat and automatically record songs at dawn and dusk everyday for weeks at a time. \nNorth Carolina Wildlife Federation is looking for volunteers to join us in the field. The Craggie Mountains are known for their rugged terrain\, steep slopes and mature forests. Volunteers will be expected to hike 5 + miles off trail in sometimes physically challenging conditions to reach target sites and install ARUs. Volunteers will start with a team lead and training will be provided. \nNCWF will be leading volunteers in the field on – \nThursday\, 4/23\nThursday\, 5/7\nThursday\, 5/21\nThursday\, 6/4\nThursday\, 6/18\nThursday\, 7/2\nThursday\, 7/16\nThursday\, 7/30\nThursday\, 8/13\nThursday\, 8/27 \nWe’ll start by 9AM and spend 6 to 7 hours in the field. Carpooling from the Asheville area will be available. Please email Luke Bennett luke@ncwf.org if you are interested in volunteering and we’ll be in touch with more information – what to bring\, where to meet\, etc. See you out there!
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/cerulean-warbler-avian-diversity-study-9/
CATEGORIES:Featured
END:VEVENT
