DTEND:20260804T193000Z
DESCRIPTION:Data Matters™ is a week-long series of one and two-day online
  courses aimed at students and professionals in business\, research\, and 
 government. The short course series is sponsored by the Odum Institute for
  Research in Social Science at UNC-Chapel Hill. Attendees get the chance t
 o learn about a wide range of topics in data science\, analytics\, visuali
 zation\, and more from expert instructors. Data Matters 2026 will be held 
 virtually\, August 3-7\, 2026. Zoom link and welcome packet will be emaile
 d shortly before the event for those registered. For a full listing of cou
 rses and registration\, visit https://odum.unc.edu/data-matters/
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Data Matters Workshop Series
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/data-matters-workshop-series
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar Group Gregg Museum Of Art Design": "https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/a-creek-in-carolina-artworks-by-bobby-c-martin"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_group_gregg_museum_of_art_design
X-SOURCE:NC State Gregg Museum of Art & Design
DTSTAMP:20260712T033930Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52629096255770
DTSTART:20260804T140000Z
DTEND:20260804T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:A Creek in Carolina: Artworks by Bobby C. Martin will be on dis
 play at the Gregg Museum of Art & Design every Tuesday-Saturday until Sept
 . 26.  The solo exhibition traces the pathways connecting ancestral Mvskok
 e homelands to Indian territory. Drawing from family photographs and archi
 val materials\, Martin (Muscogee Creek) weaves encaustic\, collage\, maps\
 , hymns and personal imagery to reframe histories of forced removal as sto
 ries of resilience\, survival and continuity — inviting viewers to refle
 ct on their own family histories and the enduring presence of Mvskoke peop
 le.
GEO:35.784762;-78.661636
LOCATION:Gregg Museum of Art & Design
SUMMARY:A Creek in Carolina: Artworks by Bobby C. Martin
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/a-creek-in-carolina-artworks-
 by-bobby-c-martin
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar Group Gregg Museum Of Art Design": "https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/stories-told-by-breath-native-american-voices-in-north-carolina"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_group_gregg_museum_of_art_design
X-SOURCE:NC State Gregg Museum of Art & Design
DTSTAMP:20260712T033930Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52426881925734
DTSTART:20260804T140000Z
DTEND:20260804T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:Stories Told by Breath will be on display at the Gregg Museum o
 f Art & Design every Tuesday-Saturday until Sept. 26. This exhibition cele
 brates the creativity\, memory and cultural continuity of Native American 
 artists connected to North Carolina. The exhibition brings together a rich
  range of media — clay\, beadwork\, textiles\, printmaking\, regalia\, s
 culpture and multimedia — woven with storytelling to form a vibrant expe
 rience of artistic practice in North Carolina. The exhibition features wor
 k by the following artists:\n\nSenora Lynch (Haliwa-Saponi)Karina McMillan
  (Lumbee)Harlen Chavis (Lumbee)Aaron Baumgardner (Catawba)Coda Cavalier (O
 ccaneechi Band of the Saponi Nation)Amy Postoak (Eastern Band of Cherokee 
 Indians) and Johnny Postoak (Muscogee Creek) of Three Sisters DesignsRhian
 non “Skye” Tafoya (Eastern Band of Cherokee and Santa Clara Pueblo)Jos
 hua Adams (Eastern Band of Cherokee)Idalis Dial (Coharie)Tim Locklear (Lum
 bee)NC State students Ashtyn Thomas (Lumbee) and Victoria Wilson (Haliwa-S
 aponi)Gwen Locklear (Lumbee)Alexandra Williams (portrait photographs of Po
 wwows at Dix Park)Together\, these artists explore heritage\, craft and st
 orytelling as a living continuum of creativity\, connecting ancestral know
 ledge with contemporary expression.
GEO:35.784762;-78.661636
LOCATION:Gregg Museum of Art & Design
SUMMARY:Stories Told by Breath: Native American Voices in North Carolina
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/stories-told-by-breath-native
 -american-voices-in-north-carolina
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_41d85e1478a55e3b4adbf2e4951c5be9f6e49241ac55a65427c71d252849bf1c
SUMMARY:No Tyranny Tuesdays: Raleigh Brier Creek
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260804T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260804T173000
DTSTAMP:20260712T033906Z
UID:3feab4l4s1qbjuk8eq5c5k91ci@google.com__20260804
SEQUENCE:3
CREATED:20251010T141943Z
DESCRIPTION:<span><p>Please join Engaged Defenders for Democracy every Tue
 sday 3:30-5:00 pm at Brier Creek on corner with Starbucks: 7854 Alexander 
 Prom Pl\, Raleigh\, NC 27617\; please park at Walmart.</p><p>This will be 
 a POSITIVE and nonviolent demonstration. We are here to protect our democr
 acy. We are standing up for what we believe in. We want to inspire people 
 to join us and grow our movement!</p><p>Please bring positive signs only. 
 Some examples: Instead of "Stop defunding science" Say "Protect Research" 
 "Immigrants make us stronger" "Housing for all" "Healthcare for all" "Save
  the planet"</p><p>Make signs about what you're standing up for -- whether
  that is the libraries\, DEI\, healthcare\, women’s rights</p><p>Please 
 no mocking signs\, no swastikas</p><p>We are excited to see you there and 
 stand together for our country!</p><p>See you every Tuesday engaging drive
 rs at Brier Creek in Raleigh.</p><p>Please join our Substack:<span> </spa
 n><a href="https://substack.com/profile/115484101-engaged-defenders-4-demo
 cracy">https://substack.com/profile/115484101-engaged-defenders-4-democrac
 y</a></p><p>For more ED4D Mobilize Events:<span> </span><a href="https://
 www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfordemocracy/">https://www.mobilize.us/enga
 gedefendersfordemocracy/</a></p><p><a href="https://www.mobilize.us/engage
 defendersfordemocracy/event/843280/">https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefende
 rsfordemocracy/event/843280/</a> </p></span>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260306T223112Z
LOCATION:7854 Alexander Prom Pl\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27617
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Durham Resistance (In Person)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_41d85e1478a55e3b4adbf2e4951c5be9f6e49241ac55a65427c71d252849bf1c
SUMMARY:Protect Democracy Tuesdays: East Club Blvd & North Roxboro St
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260804T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260804T173000
DTSTAMP:20260712T033906Z
UID:vneiglfb4b8hjnt655s58im8qk@google.com__20260804
SEQUENCE:3
CREATED:20251010T141743Z
DESCRIPTION:<span><p>Join Engaged Defenders for Democracy every Tuesday to
  the corner of E. Club and Roxboro from 4:30-5:30 to defend our democracy.
  We hold signs and encourage folks to contact their representatives. Bring
  signs that show your concern or are a call to action. Add your voice to d
 emocracy's choir! If you've never done this before\, we're happy to help y
 ou and have extra signs for you. Bring a friend and have some fun! Park in
  the SE corner parking lot.</p><p>Please join our Substack:<span> </span>
 <a href="https://substack.com/@engaged">https://substack.com/@engaged</a><
 span> </span>Defenders fordemocracy</p><p>For more ED4D Mobilize Events:<
 span> </span><a href="https://www.mobilize.us/engageddurhamitesfordemocra
 cy/">https://www.mobilize.us/engageddurhamitesfordemocracy/</a></p><p>Ven 
 todos los martes a la esquina de E. Club y Roxboro para defender nuestra d
 emocracia. Llevamos carteles y animamos a la gente a contactar a sus repre
 sentantes. Trae carteles que muestren tu preocupación o que sean un llama
 do a la acción. Añade tu voz al coro de la democracia! Si nunca lo has h
 echo\, con gusto te ayudamos y tenemos carteles adicionales para ti. Trae 
 a un amigo y diviértete! Estaciona en el estacionamiento de la esquina su
 reste.</p><p>Por favor\, vaya a nuestro Substack:<span> </span><a href="h
 ttps://substack.com/@engageddurhamitesfordemocracy">https://substack.com/@
 engageddurhamitesfordemocracy</a></p><p>For more ED4D Mobilize Events:<spa
 n> </span><a href="https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfordemocracy/">
 https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfordemocracy/</a></p><p><a href="ht
 tps://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfordemocracy/event/842822/">https://w
 ww.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfordemocracy/event/842822/</a> </p></span>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260306T223133Z
LOCATION:East Club Boulevard & North Roxboro Street\, Durham\, NC\, 27704
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Durham Resistance (In Person)
END:VEVENT
