UID:7vihpmeg1k6esqp5s5vsvq9hfe_R20260110T150000@google.com__20260815
SEQUENCE:1
CREATED:20251010T141601Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Please join Engaged Defenders for Democracy every Saturday 
 from 10am-11:30am with signs to protect our democracy and protest the viol
 ations to our Constitution. We will meet at the YMCA at 218 West Morgan St
 .</p><p>We need to fight for our democracy and stop and prevent future cut
 s that are hurting many. Bring friends! Bring signs that show your concern
  or are a call to action. Please avoid triggering images like swastikas.</
 p><p>See you every Saturday morning engaging drivers &amp\; pedestrians in
  Downtown Durham!</p><p>Please join our Substack:<span> </span><a href="h
 ttps://substack.com/profile/115484101-engaged-defenders-4-democracy">https
 ://substack.com/profile/115484101-engaged-defenders-4-democracy</a></p><p>
 For more ED4D Mobilize Events:<span> </span><a href="https://www.mobilize
 .us/engagedefendersfordemocracy/">https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersf
 ordemocracy/</a></p><p><a href="https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfor
 democracy/event/842514/">https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfordemocra
 cy/event/842514/</a> </p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260108T021307Z
LOCATION:218 W Morgan St\, Durham\, NC\, 27701
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Durham Resistance (In Person)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/the-wellness-exchange-interactive-cancer-wellness-symposium"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260712T033737Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52832758929285
DTSTART:20260815T123000Z
DTEND:20260815T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:The Wellness Exchange is an immersive\, interactive wellness sy
 mposium for people with cancer\, their caregivers\, and their adult family
  members. During the Wellness Exchange\, participants will have the opport
 unity to learn from guest speakers\, laugh with a comedian\, practice well
 ness through art and writing therapy\, move their bodies with yoga and exe
 rcise\, and rest through meditation\, mindfulness\, and reiki. During lunc
 h\, we will hear from NFL Legend Chris Draft and winningest ACC women's ba
 sketball coach Sylvia Hatchell. Participants will choose the sessions they
  wish to attend during the day. Breakfast and lunch will be served.\n\n \n
 \nFor registration and more informaton visit: https://www.activeaftercance
 r.org/wellnessexchange or contact Carly Bailey- Carly_Bailey@med.unc.edu
GEO:35.899895;-79.012764
LOCATION:The Friday Center
SUMMARY:The Wellness Exchange- Interactive Cancer Wellness Symposium 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/the-wellness-exchange-interact
 ive-cancer-wellness-symposium
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
CATEGORIES:Meetings and Conferences
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar Group Gregg Museum Of Art Design": "https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/a-creek-in-carolina-artworks-by-bobby-c-martin"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_group_gregg_museum_of_art_design
X-SOURCE:NC State Gregg Museum of Art & Design
DTSTAMP:20260712T033930Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52629096271139
DTSTART:20260815T140000Z
DTEND:20260815T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:A Creek in Carolina: Artworks by Bobby C. Martin will be on dis
 play at the Gregg Museum of Art & Design every Tuesday-Saturday until Sept
 . 26.  The solo exhibition traces the pathways connecting ancestral Mvskok
 e homelands to Indian territory. Drawing from family photographs and archi
 val materials\, Martin (Muscogee Creek) weaves encaustic\, collage\, maps\
 , hymns and personal imagery to reframe histories of forced removal as sto
 ries of resilience\, survival and continuity — inviting viewers to refle
 ct on their own family histories and the enduring presence of Mvskoke peop
 le.
GEO:35.784762;-78.661636
LOCATION:Gregg Museum of Art & Design
SUMMARY:A Creek in Carolina: Artworks by Bobby C. Martin
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/a-creek-in-carolina-artworks-
 by-bobby-c-martin
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar Group Gregg Museum Of Art Design": "https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/stories-told-by-breath-native-american-voices-in-north-carolina"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_group_gregg_museum_of_art_design
X-SOURCE:NC State Gregg Museum of Art & Design
DTSTAMP:20260712T033930Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52629330029348
DTSTART:20260815T140000Z
DTEND:20260815T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:Stories Told by Breath will be on display at the Gregg Museum o
 f Art & Design every Tuesday-Saturday until Sept. 26. This exhibition cele
 brates the creativity\, memory and cultural continuity of Native American 
 artists connected to North Carolina. The exhibition brings together a rich
  range of media — clay\, beadwork\, textiles\, printmaking\, regalia\, s
 culpture and multimedia — woven with storytelling to form a vibrant expe
 rience of artistic practice in North Carolina. The exhibition features wor
 k by the following artists:\n\nSenora Lynch (Haliwa-Saponi)Karina McMillan
  (Lumbee)Harlen Chavis (Lumbee)Aaron Baumgardner (Catawba)Coda Cavalier (O
 ccaneechi Band of the Saponi Nation)Amy Postoak (Eastern Band of Cherokee 
 Indians) and Johnny Postoak (Muscogee Creek) of Three Sisters DesignsRhian
 non “Skye” Tafoya (Eastern Band of Cherokee and Santa Clara Pueblo)Jos
 hua Adams (Eastern Band of Cherokee)Idalis Dial (Coharie)Tim Locklear (Lum
 bee)NC State students Ashtyn Thomas (Lumbee) and Victoria Wilson (Haliwa-S
 aponi)Gwen Locklear (Lumbee)Alexandra Williams (portrait photographs of Po
 wwows at Dix Park)Together\, these artists explore heritage\, craft and st
 orytelling as a living continuum of creativity\, connecting ancestral know
 ledge with contemporary expression.
GEO:35.784762;-78.661636
LOCATION:Gregg Museum of Art & Design
SUMMARY:Stories Told by Breath: Native American Voices in North Carolina
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/stories-told-by-breath-native
 -american-voices-in-north-carolina
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
