BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gardens": "https://gardens.duke.edu/event/steeped-in-culture-a-summer-season-chinese-tea-tasting/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gardens
X-SOURCE:Sarah P. Duke Gardens
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260822T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260822T120000
DTSTAMP:20260706T121153Z
CREATED:20260706T121153Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260706T121153Z
UID:17430-1787392800-1787400000@gardens.duke.edu
SUMMARY:Steeped in Culture: A Summer Season Chinese Tea Tasting
DESCRIPTION:Experience tea as a social beverage and cultural tradition on this seasonal sensory journey with Violet Yang of Forest Well Tea. Participants will taste four different Chinese loose-leaf teas and be guided through experiencing the aromas\, colors\, textures and evolving flavors. Together\, you’ll explore the plant\, history\, processing methods\, regional origins\, brewing techniques and cultural stories behind each tea. Designed to be approachable\, sensory and educational\, this session offers a quiet moment to slow down\, connect and discover the depth of tea through taste and story.\n \nFee: $38; 20% discount for Duke Gardens members with discount code. \nParking: Parking fees apply.\n \nLocation: Pelham-Cullen Classroom inside the Barnes Welcome Center.\n \nAccessibility: This program takes place seated in an indoor location accessible via paved surfaces and equipped with a hearing loop\, which transmits sound directly to hearing aids and cochlear implants with a T-coil setting. Accessible restrooms are available onsite.
URL:https://gardens.duke.edu/event/steeped-in-culture-a-summer-season-chinese-tea-tasting/
LOCATION:Duke Gardens–Pelham-Cullen Classroom in the Barnes Welcome Center\, 420 Anderson Street\, Durham\, NC\, 27705\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adult Programs
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://gardens.duke.edu/wp-content/uploads/tea-summer.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_41d85e1478a55e3b4adbf2e4951c5be9f6e49241ac55a65427c71d252849bf1c
SUMMARY:Defend Democracy Saturdays: Downtown Durham
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260822T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260822T113000
DTSTAMP:20260712T033906Z
UID:7vihpmeg1k6esqp5s5vsvq9hfe_R20260110T150000@google.com__20260822
SEQUENCE:1
CREATED:20251010T141601Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Please join Engaged Defenders for Democracy every Saturday 
 from 10am-11:30am with signs to protect our democracy and protest the viol
 ations to our Constitution. We will meet at the YMCA at 218 West Morgan St
 .</p><p>We need to fight for our democracy and stop and prevent future cut
 s that are hurting many. Bring friends! Bring signs that show your concern
  or are a call to action. Please avoid triggering images like swastikas.</
 p><p>See you every Saturday morning engaging drivers &amp\; pedestrians in
  Downtown Durham!</p><p>Please join our Substack:<span> </span><a href="h
 ttps://substack.com/profile/115484101-engaged-defenders-4-democracy">https
 ://substack.com/profile/115484101-engaged-defenders-4-democracy</a></p><p>
 For more ED4D Mobilize Events:<span> </span><a href="https://www.mobilize
 .us/engagedefendersfordemocracy/">https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersf
 ordemocracy/</a></p><p><a href="https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfor
 democracy/event/842514/">https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfordemocra
 cy/event/842514/</a> </p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260108T021307Z
LOCATION:218 W Morgan St\, Durham\, NC\, 27701
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Durham Resistance (In Person)
END:VEVENT
