DESCRIPTION:A guided look at African textiles on view in Continental Shift: Recent Acquisitions of African Art and the Museum’s African art collection gallery. \nLed by Dr. Victoria Rovine\, Department of Art and Art History and Carolina Public Humanities\, Millie West\, PhD student (Department of Art and Art History)\, and Nancy Andoh\, PhD student (Department of History). Free\, but space is limited; registration required below. \nThis event is part of UNC–Chapel Hill’s Campus Life Experience (CLE) program. Students who attend can scan the QR code provided at the event to receive CLE credit.
