BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ackland Art Museum": "https://events.ackland.org/event/ackland-film-forum-set-it-off-f-gary-gray-1996/", "UNC Chapel Hill": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/ackland-film-forum-set-it-off-f-gary-gray-1996"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.ackland.org/event/ackland-film-forum-set-it-off-f-gary-gray-1996/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
X-SOURCE:Ackland Art Museum, UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261005T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261005T210000
DTSTAMP:20260711T233859
CREATED:20260708T192201Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260708T192201Z
UID:10004446-1791228600-1791234000@events.ackland.org
SUMMARY:Ackland Film Forum: "Set It Off" (F. Gary Gray\, 1996)
DESCRIPTION:Jada Pinkett Smith\, Queen Latifah\, and Vivica A. Fox anchor this energetic reworking of the heist film. After a series of setbacks leaves four Black women with few viable paths forward\, they embark on a string of increasingly audacious bank robberies. Blending humor\, suspense\, and tragedy\, Set It Off captures both the bonds of friendship and the pressures of race\, gender\, and economic inequality in 1990s urban America. \nThis film will be introduced by Professor Daelena Tinnin-Gadson\, UNC-Chapel Hill Department of English and Comparative Literature. \nIt will be screened at 7:30 p.m. at The Lumina Theater (620 Market St\, Chapel Hill\, NC 27516). Tickets are free for all audience members\, and registration is required via The Lumina’s webpage. When this link is live\, click to reserve your free ticket. \nUNC-Chapel Hill students can receive CLE credit for attending by scanning the QR code at the event. \n  \nAbout the Series: \nJoin the Ackland Film Forum this fall for Crime Thrillers from the Americas: Snapshots of Social Anxiety\, a series that accompanies the Ackland exhibition Care and Concern: Recent Acquisitions of Modern and Contemporary Art. \nAs vehicles of social commentary and stylistic bravura\, crime thrillers often register the pressures and contradictions of their historical moment. Across nearly half a century\, the films in this series stage encounters with political power\, public trust\, inequality\, and ambition through assassination plots\, botched robberies\, and media-driven spectacle. \nFrom the crises of the late 1960s to the intensified media environments of the twenty-first century\, these works show how genre cinema can capture social anxiety in real time. Each film stands both as a gripping narrative and as a record of a world under strain\, where institutions falter and everyday life becomes fraught with conflict. \nThe Ackland Film Forum is co-organized by the Ackland Art Museum and UNC Film Studies\, housed in the UNC-Chapel Hill Department of English and Comparative Literature.
URL:https://events.ackland.org/event/ackland-film-forum-set-it-off-f-gary-gray-1996/
LOCATION:The Lumina Theater\, 620 Market Street\, Chapel Hill\, 27516\, United States
CATEGORIES:Ackland Film Forum
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.ackland.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/e9bfd41f-full.jpg
END:VEVENT
